compat: keep libc headers out of the freestanding loader build

compat.h fills in constants an old or minimal libc may lack, and defines
SYS_SECCOMP among them. glibc declares that name in an enumeration, so a
translation unit that reaches compat.h before <signal.h> turns the
enumerator into a numeric constant and fails to compile. Include the
header first where there is one to include: the loader is built
freestanding and must keep doing without it.

Offered upstream; drop this file once it lands.
diff --git a/src/compat.h b/src/compat.h
index 53300b8..2ffd05b 100644
--- a/src/compat.h
+++ b/src/compat.h
@@ -23,6 +23,11 @@
 #ifndef COMPAT_H
 #define COMPAT_H
 
+/* The loader is built freestanding and must not pull in libc headers. */
+#if __STDC_HOSTED__
+#    include <signal.h>  /* SYS_SECCOMP, which the fallback below would shadow */
+#endif
+
 /* Local definitions for compatibility with old and/or broken distros... */
 #    ifndef AT_NULL
 #        define AT_NULL			0
